{"kind":"assert","text":"Order, Hugh 20 November 21:34 EST: the workroom restarts, and the live level goes first. Build LV2 to LV5 (fresh requests LV2 8af903e9, LV3 a76e3655, LV4 627719c9, LV5 f5b39d57; the requests of 13 November went stale in the cleanup of 18 November, and my act 34adeab1 rested on one of them, so this act replaces it) per notes/2026-11-10-live-level.md section 8. LV1 landed in 1f81ac01. This act amends the order of 5c7c0074: the live lanes come before LA-2, LA-3, LA-4 and CJ-1.\n\nLanes, in parallel subagents, each with its own worktree, branch and promise:\nA. LV2, the live turn (sections 3.3, 3.4, 3.6, 3.7). Promise it now and start. It removes the `derivable` refusal of ruling a1fe9aaf, so runtime creation of a live scope works when it lands.\nB. The graph part of LV4: the package graph's entry for a live scope and the refusal of a send to one. It needs only LV1, so it starts now beside A.\nC. LV3, reads and the watch (section 3.5). Write it stacked on the LV2 branch as soon as the turn's interfaces hold still; do not wait for the LV2 landing to start writing. It gates after LV2 lands.\nD. The tool part of LV4 (the app-only MCP tool, the client call, `dap act`) follows LV3. LV5 is last.\n\nRulings on the open points of section 11:\n- O2: a live scope answers `unavailable` to a delivery that arrives after its confirmation, as proposed. LV2 shows in a test that the sender's own deadline settles its request.\n- O1 and O3 stay with LV3 as proposed: a byte bound from the definition's item limits with `scope-full`, stated as a change to `contract`; and a measurement of what the host does with an idle live scope under an open watch, with no promise either way.\n- O4 as proposed. O5 does not block these heads: none adds a form that waits.\n\nGate slot: one gate at a time, as before. A live head that is ready takes the next slot ahead of every other lane. While no live head is ready, LA-2 then LA-3 may use the slot; do not let them delay a ready live 